## How to Run the Project

Follow these steps to get the API running on your local machine:

### 1. Installation

Open your terminal in the project root folder (`blog-api`) and install the necessary dependencies:

```bash
npm install

```

### 2. Start the Server

Run the application using Node.js:

```bash
node server.js

```

You should see the message: `Server started on port 3000`.

### 3. Testing the API

Use **Postman** to interact with the following endpoints:

1. Create a Post (POST Method)
This proves your API can receive data and save it.

URL: http://localhost:3000/api/posts

Method: POST

Body (JSON): ```json
{
"title": "Learning Express API",
"content": "This is a detailed description to ensure I pass the validation of twenty characters.",
"author": "Anusha"
}

Look for: 201 Created status and the generated id and timestamps.

2. Get All Posts with Pagination (GET Method)
This proves your pagination and query parameter logic is working.

URL: http://localhost:3000/api/posts?page=1&limit=5

Method: GET

Look for: 200 OK status and the JSON object containing totalPosts, totalPages, and the posts array.

3. Title Validation Error (400 Bad Request)
This proves you have implemented the "min 5 chars" requirement.

URL: http://localhost:3000/api/posts

Method: POST

Body (JSON): ```json
{
"title": "Bad",
"content": "This content is long enough, but the title is too short.",
"author": "Anusha"
}

Look for: 400 Bad Request status and the message Error: Title must be min 5 chars.

4. Content Validation Error (400 Bad Request)
This proves you have implemented the "min 20 chars" requirement.

URL: http://localhost:3000/api/posts

Method: POST

Body (JSON): ```json
{
"title": "Perfect Title Name",
"content": "Too short.",
"author": "Anusha"
}

Look for: 400 Bad Request status and the message Error: Content must be min 20 chars.

5. Invalid ID Error (404 Not Found)
This proves your "Handle edge cases" requirement for missing posts.

URL: http://localhost:3000/api/posts/99999

Method: GET

Look for: 404 Not Found status and the message Post not found.

6. Delete a Post (DELETE Method)
This proves the final part of your CRUD operations.

URL: http://localhost:3000/api/posts/1780469619438.

Method: DELETE

Look for: 200 OK status and the message Post deleted successfully.

7. Middleware Logging (VS Code Terminal)
This proves your "Use middleware for logging" requirement.

Action: Look your VS Code Terminal window.

